Looking at how `Inbox` works: `Inbox.__init__(gate, capture, effect, rules, routes, clock, name)`. The `capture(request)` reads premises from systems of record, `effect(request)` builds the effect payload. `Inbox._proposal` builds `{agent, lease, request_id, premises, effect, request}`.

Task 3.1 asks for `effect(request)` and `capture(request)` per action; 3.2 wires one Inbox per action family. The action families are: payments (reissue_payment + refund_fee share the payment rail), scheduler (book_appointment), case-records (change_address).

